<title>TURKEY: Turk Sise-Cam 9-mth profit jump 146 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Sise-Cam 9-mth profit jump 146 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	  420.11  vs     416.62</p>
<p>    Net profit			 2,352.64  vs     958.22</p>
<p>    Net sales			    754.23  vs     358.68</p>
<p>    Operating loss			46.51  vs	 5.18</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	     2,722.41  vs   1,236.73</p>
<p>    Interest paid			  0.70  vs	94.27</p>
<p>    Total debts			1,708.56  vs     968.14</p>
<p>    Equity			    10,599.51  vs   5,522.27</p>
<p>    Capital			    5,600.00  vs   2,300.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkiye Sise ve Cam Fabrikalari A.S., owned 74.91 percent by leading commercial T.Is Bankas A.S., is the parent company of Turkey's biggest glass and glassware producing and marketing group.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
